WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.007
[opening theme song playing]

00:45.086 --> 00:48.882
[plane rumbling]

00:52.260 --> 00:54.262
[sentimental music]

01:01.519 --> 01:03.730
100 YEARS OF MODERN METEOROLOGY
NEW CHALLENGES

01:11.780 --> 01:13.448
[Si-woo] Relationships evolve.

01:13.531 --> 01:18.745
[camera shutter clicking]

01:19.704 --> 01:22.665
[Si-woo] It can make them stronger
or make them fall apart.

01:23.625 --> 01:25.877
- The changes depend on time.
- [sighs heavily]

01:27.128 --> 01:31.925
And how each person's emotions build,
with or against their partner.

01:32.801 --> 01:35.094
[camera shutter clicks]

01:35.178 --> 01:37.305
- Mm, we need the food too.
- Oh!

01:37.388 --> 01:39.182
- Like that?
- Ah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:39.849 --> 01:43.269
[camera shutter clicking]

01:52.403 --> 01:53.822
[cabin crew] Ladies and gentlemen,

01:53.905 --> 01:57.742
we are beginning our descent
to Jeju International Airport.

01:57.826 --> 02:01.538
Please fasten your seatbelts
and open the shade to your windows.

02:01.621 --> 02:02.789
Thank you.

02:02.872 --> 02:04.207
[window shades open]

02:08.336 --> 02:09.754
[Si-woo] What's scary is…

02:10.547 --> 02:12.674
I want things to work out.

02:14.759 --> 02:17.512
I want things to work out
for the two of us.

02:18.388 --> 02:19.514
But…

02:21.391 --> 02:23.184
that's the only thing.

02:25.728 --> 02:30.567
Although that stays under control
with tempered feelings.

02:30.650 --> 02:32.986
I like it simple and stable.

02:34.529 --> 02:37.073
If things start to go beyond moderate,

02:38.825 --> 02:40.326
I become anxious.

02:43.830 --> 02:45.248
Then I feel…

02:46.416 --> 02:48.585
I become someone else and not myself.

02:54.048 --> 02:55.758
Get up. Let's take you back home.

02:56.926 --> 02:58.761
So then you should decide.

03:00.305 --> 03:02.724
You should decide while you're in Jeju.

03:07.896 --> 03:11.190
[sighs]
If you think you can do it moderately

03:11.274 --> 03:12.901
or not.

03:12.984 --> 03:15.445
Really think about it, then decide.

03:18.072 --> 03:20.116
["I Love You This Much" by Punch playing]

03:20.199 --> 03:23.286
[Si-woo] Knowing little misunderstandings
and disagreements

03:23.912 --> 03:27.123
pushed the evolution,
and we don't notice it.

03:28.124 --> 03:31.252
And we can fall
out of sync with each other.

03:32.837 --> 03:36.090
All I really wanted was a moment.

03:36.925 --> 03:38.259
Like this.

03:39.427 --> 03:42.430
To have time to realign and be together.

03:47.393 --> 03:49.395
["I Love You This Much" by Punch playing]

04:00.073 --> 04:03.284
[Si-woo] I must have missed
where we fell out.

04:05.828 --> 04:11.292
How did we end up looking down a path

04:12.335 --> 04:16.172
with no idea of what awaits us?

04:22.929 --> 04:26.391
EPISODE 12
VARIATION AREA

04:26.474 --> 04:30.770
WHEN A HOT TYPHOON CHANGES
AS IT PASSES THROUGH KOREA'S COLD AIR

04:30.853 --> 04:34.732
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

04:35.984 --> 04:37.193
[Ha-kyung sniffs]

04:44.158 --> 04:46.035
Thank you.
[clears throat]

04:46.119 --> 04:47.245
[blows nose]

04:50.331 --> 04:52.709
I didn't realize you are so invested.

04:53.376 --> 04:54.836
Who knows what I feel?

04:55.586 --> 04:58.172
It seems like everything is falling apart.

05:01.217 --> 05:02.260
[sighs]

05:03.803 --> 05:05.013
[exhales heavily]

05:07.890 --> 05:10.560
Director! Where's your phone?
We've been calling you.

05:10.643 --> 05:12.895
- We couldn't reach you.
- Is there something wrong?

05:13.813 --> 05:15.565
The Situation Room is in chaos.

05:15.648 --> 05:17.066
You have to go right now.

05:18.651 --> 05:20.903
I want to talk to the guy in charge.

05:21.487 --> 05:23.614
Damn it, bring me your boss, okay?

05:23.698 --> 05:25.616
- Don't you film this!
- Okay, okay, we understand.

05:25.700 --> 05:26.909
I need you to calm down.

05:26.993 --> 05:28.661
You can talk to someone outside.

05:28.745 --> 05:31.706
Outside? You think I can calm down
and leave right now

05:31.789 --> 05:34.834
when my only kid's bleeding out
in the hospital somewhere?

05:34.917 --> 05:37.545
No information. He's dead for all I know!

05:37.628 --> 05:40.631
I'm worried out of my mind,
and you say, "Just calm down"?

05:41.215 --> 05:44.260
For Christ's sake! Is this funny?
Is this a joke to you?

05:44.343 --> 05:45.845
I can't calm down!

05:45.928 --> 05:47.930
How will what you're doing help your son?

05:48.014 --> 05:49.807
What? Are you the boss man?

05:49.891 --> 05:51.350
Huh? Back off.

05:51.434 --> 05:53.394
- Back off!
- [Ha-kyung] What's going on?

05:55.980 --> 05:57.940
Oh. It's you.

05:59.025 --> 06:00.902
I'm Director Jin Ha-kyung of Team Two.

06:00.985 --> 06:02.445
I'm Mr. Lee's supervisor.

06:02.528 --> 06:04.280
[Myung-han] Right. Director Lady.

06:05.406 --> 06:08.034
You hear what happened?
They let my boy get hurt.

06:08.868 --> 06:09.869
Yes.

06:09.952 --> 06:13.081
Someone from Jeju called
and said he's in the hospital.

06:13.164 --> 06:16.417
I couldn't breathe.
My heart was gonna beat out of my chest.

06:16.501 --> 06:18.711
I couldn't see. I blacked out!

06:18.795 --> 06:20.838
I can discuss it with you outside of here.

06:20.922 --> 06:23.091
We don't allow civilians
in the Situation Room.

06:23.174 --> 06:24.217
For real?

06:24.300 --> 06:25.760
Finally, please get him out.

06:25.843 --> 06:27.887
- [officer] Come here, man.
- Shit. Stay away.

06:27.970 --> 06:29.931
You want some of this? You can't touch me!

06:30.014 --> 06:32.350
Don't try it! Just stay away!

06:32.934 --> 06:34.435
[employees clamor]

06:34.519 --> 06:36.562
[Myung-han] I have rights. Don't touch me.

06:36.646 --> 06:38.397
You're attacking me!

06:38.481 --> 06:40.066
I'll sue everyone here!

06:43.444 --> 06:44.487
I got it.

06:45.238 --> 06:46.280
[Ki-jun] Hello, sir.

06:47.281 --> 06:49.325
What you're doing
is obstructing official duties.

06:49.408 --> 06:51.327
[scoffs]
What, so?

06:51.410 --> 06:52.662
Are you going to sue me, then?

06:52.745 --> 06:54.539
[Ki-jun] I'm just trying to explain to you

06:54.622 --> 06:56.624
that it's important
that they can do their work.

06:56.707 --> 06:59.669
It's not the place to show up
and make demands. Understand?

06:59.752 --> 07:01.546
- Hey!
- [Ki-jun] Okay, you can talk to me.

07:01.629 --> 07:03.131
My boy is important, too.

07:03.214 --> 07:05.299
[Myung-han] He's the only son
for two generations in a row.

07:05.383 --> 07:06.843
He's all I got!

07:06.926 --> 07:08.219
Damn it.

07:11.222 --> 07:12.473
[sighs]

07:12.557 --> 07:14.142
Our Lady Director knows best.

07:14.225 --> 07:17.145
You personally know my son's important.

07:17.228 --> 07:18.396
You're close, right?

07:20.481 --> 07:22.692
[tense music]

07:26.154 --> 07:29.615
I'm referring to seeing you and my son

07:29.699 --> 07:32.410
being close enough
to hit the motel together.

07:37.457 --> 07:38.374
Ah.

07:38.458 --> 07:40.543
I see. No one knows.

07:42.003 --> 07:43.421
[chuckles]
Okay, okay, I get it.

07:43.504 --> 07:45.590
I won't talk too loud.

07:46.674 --> 07:47.675
[chuckles nervously]

07:48.301 --> 07:53.306
Anyway, it's true that… that you two
are in a relationship, then?

07:58.394 --> 08:00.480
Well, I know what I saw in that motel.

08:02.982 --> 08:04.901
You guys see each other, right?

08:08.070 --> 08:09.363
[Ki-jun exhales heavily]

08:09.447 --> 08:10.740
That's enough.

08:12.325 --> 08:13.868
What, she's got nothing to say?

08:15.786 --> 08:17.830
We're going outside.
We'll talk there, okay?

08:22.376 --> 08:23.252
Sure, let's go.

08:23.878 --> 08:25.421
[Myung-han] We've got lots to discuss.

08:35.515 --> 08:38.142
I can handle this.
Don't feel like you have to be there.

08:40.144 --> 08:42.146
[tense music]

08:51.739 --> 08:52.615
[Myung-ju] Oh.

09:07.713 --> 09:09.090
[sighs]

09:09.173 --> 09:10.299
[exhales heavily]

09:11.050 --> 09:12.969
[thunder rumbling]

09:14.554 --> 09:16.514
- Mr. Um.
- [Dong-han] Hm?

09:19.600 --> 09:21.227
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

09:21.310 --> 09:23.938
Wow, when did that start, huh?

09:24.021 --> 09:26.023
[foreboding music]

09:27.400 --> 09:29.735
[phone ringing]

09:31.779 --> 09:33.948
Hello. Headquarters. This is Um.

09:34.031 --> 09:35.408
We just saw it.

09:36.033 --> 09:37.368
Is it a…

09:37.451 --> 09:41.247
Typhoon, yes. Number 15 Elisha,
that was following Number 14 Ricky.

09:41.330 --> 09:45.459
[Mi-jin] Around eleven o'clock today,
it was moving northeastward,

09:45.543 --> 09:48.629
300km near Okinawa,
the central pressure was 990,

09:48.713 --> 09:51.757
max wind velocity, 20 per second,
and a radius of 150.

09:54.051 --> 09:56.887
[thunder rumbling]

10:03.769 --> 10:04.604
[sighs]

10:05.646 --> 10:06.981
You have a cig?

10:09.108 --> 10:10.568
There's no smoking in the building.

10:10.651 --> 10:13.154
At least give me a coffee, then.

10:15.072 --> 10:17.158
[Myung-han breathes sharply]

10:17.241 --> 10:19.577
Ah, shit. It broke on me.

10:19.660 --> 10:22.413
That's gonna cost me later. Damn it.

10:22.496 --> 10:24.206
Ah, shit.

10:25.374 --> 10:26.584
[Myung-han clicks tongue]

10:26.667 --> 10:28.002
- [thumps]
- [Myung-han sighs]

10:30.880 --> 10:33.174
[suspenseful music]

10:33.257 --> 10:34.508
[indistinct chatter]

10:34.592 --> 10:37.470
By eight o'clock tonight,
Okinawa and the nearby area

10:37.553 --> 10:40.222
should see it, 120km over the western sea,

10:40.306 --> 10:42.558
and it's heading towards
the southern Jeju sea.

10:42.642 --> 10:46.145
Central pressure is 980,
wind velocity, 28, wind radius, 200.

10:47.980 --> 10:50.024
[suspenseful music]

11:01.035 --> 11:03.245
16 HOURS AGO

11:13.381 --> 11:14.674
[sighs]

11:16.342 --> 11:17.551
[Hyang-rae] Take it slow.

11:19.428 --> 11:20.471
[Dong-han] Oh, Bo-mi.

11:21.097 --> 11:23.891
Father. Did you sleep here?

11:24.642 --> 11:26.811
Yeah. Feel better? You okay now?

11:26.894 --> 11:29.105
Yeah, I'm okay. Everything's okay.

11:29.688 --> 11:30.523
[breathes heavily]

11:30.606 --> 11:32.400
The taxi is waiting for us. Let's go.

11:32.900 --> 11:34.944
[Dong-han] Wait, you called a taxi?

11:35.027 --> 11:36.529
We can take my car.

11:37.905 --> 11:39.073
Come on, Bo-mi.

11:41.033 --> 11:43.035
[somber music]

11:44.829 --> 11:45.788
Ah.

11:51.001 --> 11:53.838
- [door closes]
- [breathes deeply]

12:01.762 --> 12:04.932
Father looked tired,
like he didn't sleep at all.

12:05.724 --> 12:08.519
Isn't it kinda rude
leaving him at the hospital like that?

12:08.602 --> 12:10.187
Since when did he

12:11.480 --> 12:13.899
start waiting for us like he cares at all?

12:13.983 --> 12:16.360
I've been waiting for over ten years.

12:16.444 --> 12:18.070
He can wait one night.

12:18.154 --> 12:20.573
[somber music]

12:24.869 --> 12:26.620
You should rest until we get back.

12:31.459 --> 12:32.501
[sighs]

12:38.424 --> 12:42.136
[breathes deeply]

12:46.474 --> 12:49.101
Let's go right now. Come and eat.

12:49.185 --> 12:50.311
[Myung-ju] Honey, breakfast.

12:50.394 --> 12:51.854
- Come on.
- It's mine!

12:51.937 --> 12:53.731
- [both grunting]
- Goodness. Hey!

12:53.814 --> 12:56.567
- Give it to me. No, let it go. Let it go.
- [grunts]

12:56.650 --> 12:58.402
[Myung-ju] Come, sit down.
Both of you. Here we go.

12:58.486 --> 12:59.820
Oh, let's eat, boys.

12:59.904 --> 13:01.614
- Your backpack's packed?
- [older son] No.

13:01.697 --> 13:02.698
Go pack it right now.

13:02.781 --> 13:05.159
Hey, we'll do this later. Later.
Let's get you dressed.

13:05.242 --> 13:07.495
Stand up. Oh…

13:08.162 --> 13:09.663
Oh, my agenda.

13:10.247 --> 13:11.540
- Aah!
- Your agenda?

13:11.624 --> 13:14.001
- Do you know where it's gone to?
- [older son] No!

13:14.084 --> 13:15.211
Did you check the floor?

13:16.003 --> 13:17.421
One more.

13:17.505 --> 13:19.757
- [coughing]
- [older son] Oh, found it!

13:19.840 --> 13:23.385
I'll get you water. Put the agenda
in your backpack, okay?

13:23.469 --> 13:25.346
- [older son] Okay.
- [younger son] Vroom, vroom!

13:25.429 --> 13:27.723
Vroom, vroom! Vroom!

13:29.808 --> 13:31.519
Honey, it's getting cold.

13:33.354 --> 13:34.313
Honey.

13:36.106 --> 13:36.982
[Jung-ho groans]

13:37.566 --> 13:39.109
He's working so hard.

13:40.110 --> 13:42.154
The Level Five exam isn't that hard.

13:44.823 --> 13:46.325
[sighs]
I'll just leave it.

13:47.243 --> 13:48.911
Come on! Boys!

13:57.878 --> 13:58.963
Hello, nice to meet you.

13:59.046 --> 14:01.090
I'm Forecaster Lee Si-woo
from Headquarters.

14:01.173 --> 14:02.174
[Mi-jin] How's it look now?

14:02.258 --> 14:04.510
When the trough gets higher
than five kilometers above ground,

14:04.593 --> 14:06.095
it should pull the typhoon.

14:06.178 --> 14:08.806
So the velocity of it will increase
between 20 and 25.

14:08.889 --> 14:10.015
[employee 1] Mm.

14:10.641 --> 14:13.394
If that's the rate,
it'll probably hit later than expected.

14:14.061 --> 14:16.438
NATIONAL TYPHOON CENTER

14:17.147 --> 14:19.608
Oh, hi, I'm Forecaster Lee Si-woo
from Headquarters.

14:19.692 --> 14:21.694
- Your prediction?
- [Si-woo] Sorry?

14:23.362 --> 14:24.363
Oh.

14:24.446 --> 14:27.783
Um, the way I see it,
the North Pacific anticyclone

14:27.867 --> 14:31.662
over by Japan is moving slower
than initially forecast.

14:31.745 --> 14:36.166
At this rate, I think it could slow down
to 10 or 15km per hour.

14:36.834 --> 14:37.793
Excuse me.

14:37.877 --> 14:40.921
Why do you think that would affect
the typhoon's course? Seems unlikely.

14:41.005 --> 14:44.675
I'm thinking of two specific cases
from 2002 and 2014,

14:44.758 --> 14:47.344
when the velocity
of the typhoon was slowed

14:47.428 --> 14:49.889
by the development
of that anticyclone in Japan.

14:51.181 --> 14:53.058
In 2014, it was Dolphin.

14:53.142 --> 14:55.436
- And in 2002…
- It was Haishen.

14:56.020 --> 15:00.441
Both cases had high variation
and turned into extratropical cyclones.

15:05.738 --> 15:06.906
And what was your name?

15:07.531 --> 15:08.365
[chuckles softly]

15:08.449 --> 15:10.784
Sorry, I'm sent
from the main Headquarters,

15:10.868 --> 15:12.453
Lee Si-woo, Severe Weather.

15:13.495 --> 15:16.123
I'm the Director. Sung Mi-jin here.

15:16.206 --> 15:17.583
Of course, nice to meet you.

15:17.666 --> 15:20.044
I should thank you for getting me here
earlier than expected.

15:21.545 --> 15:25.090
Each year, the climate totally transforms
beyond our predictions.

15:25.174 --> 15:28.302
Being here a week early
isn't enough to prepare sufficiently.

15:28.385 --> 15:29.637
What should I start with?

15:31.013 --> 15:32.014
[clicks tongue]

15:32.097 --> 15:34.266
Well, we've got a meeting in five minutes.

15:34.892 --> 15:36.101
Yes, ma'am.

15:36.185 --> 15:38.187
[uplifting music]

15:51.325 --> 15:53.494
- [Team Leader 1] Hello.
- [Team Leader 2] Hello.

15:53.577 --> 15:54.828
Hello.

15:54.912 --> 15:56.747
- Hello.
- Hello.

15:56.830 --> 15:59.333
SAFE COUNTRY, PEACEFUL PEOPLE

15:59.416 --> 16:00.250
[Soo-jin gasps]

16:00.334 --> 16:02.002
Lee Si-woo's on the screen.

16:08.175 --> 16:09.718
[Si-woo] Good morning, everyone.

16:09.802 --> 16:12.680
[Dong-han] Good morning?
There's nothing good about it.

16:12.763 --> 16:14.056
A typhoon's on its way.

16:15.057 --> 16:17.059
[Si-woo] Well,
that's an exciting morning, at least.

16:17.142 --> 16:18.435
I have great timing.

16:18.519 --> 16:20.479
I got to the typhoon center
on the right day.

16:20.562 --> 16:21.897
You're thrilled, I'm sure.

16:23.482 --> 16:27.152
My goodness, all that energy
is meant to be in the field.

16:27.736 --> 16:29.071
[employees laughing]

16:29.655 --> 16:32.116
- All right. Typhoon's coming.
- Hello, sir.

16:32.199 --> 16:33.367
- Hello, sir.
- Hello, sir.

16:33.450 --> 16:34.410
Mm.

16:34.493 --> 16:35.953
[Mi-jin] General Director.

16:36.036 --> 16:38.372
You sent someone that actually knows
what they're doing.

16:38.455 --> 16:39.623
[Bong-chan] Oh, yeah?

16:40.374 --> 16:43.460
It wasn't up to me.
Thank Director Jin for him.

16:44.253 --> 16:45.629
[Mi-jin] Director Jin Ha-kyung?

16:45.713 --> 16:48.048
Well, it's nice to get
a good surprise for once.

16:51.010 --> 16:52.594
Let's get started.

16:52.678 --> 16:54.346
Satellite Center, what's your report?

16:54.430 --> 16:57.933
[employee 2] Two typhoons are developing
far out on the sea near Okinawa.

16:58.017 --> 17:01.311
One has a central pressure of 985

17:01.395 --> 17:04.690
and a maximum sustained wind
of 25m per second.

17:05.357 --> 17:06.984
Compared to three hours ago…

17:07.067 --> 17:08.402
[Ha-kyung] I like you.

17:08.485 --> 17:10.571
[sentimental music]

17:10.654 --> 17:11.864
[chuckles softly]

17:13.073 --> 17:15.701
I really like you a lot.

17:16.535 --> 17:19.079
Everything's so difficult.

17:25.377 --> 17:26.503
[sighs]

17:26.587 --> 17:28.130
Why do you think it's difficult?

17:29.381 --> 17:31.550
We're different from each other.

17:32.968 --> 17:34.928
And I mostly like that.

17:36.638 --> 17:38.766
It's just difficult sometimes.

17:46.273 --> 17:48.734
[sentimental music]

17:53.572 --> 17:54.782
[exhales deeply]

17:54.865 --> 17:57.409
At this phase, we'll see signs of it
starting tomorrow afternoon,

17:57.493 --> 17:58.702
is that correct?

17:58.786 --> 18:00.746
[Dong-han] The moving velocity
has gone up.

18:00.829 --> 18:02.289
However, the surface temperature
in the sea out there

18:02.372 --> 18:04.249
is between 26 and 27 degrees.

18:04.333 --> 18:06.168
Quantity of the heat is less than ten.

18:06.251 --> 18:08.087
And the vertical shear
is under 10 degrees too.

18:08.170 --> 18:10.130
So I don't think we have
the right condition

18:10.214 --> 18:11.965
for the typhoon to continue developing.

18:13.634 --> 18:14.676
Typhoon Center.

18:14.760 --> 18:17.429
Any factors or theories
as to why the typhoon

18:17.513 --> 18:18.597
isn't gaining more energy?

18:19.556 --> 18:23.435
The warmest time of day is a few hours out
so the quantity of heat will rise.

18:24.019 --> 18:26.522
Especially looking at annual trend
showing the surface temperature

18:26.605 --> 18:28.148
is 3 degrees higher than last year.

18:28.232 --> 18:30.109
I would expect that the typhoon

18:30.192 --> 18:33.195
will continue gaining energy
even after entering our waters.

18:35.572 --> 18:38.367
What's its expected strength
when it travels inland?

18:38.450 --> 18:44.414
When it hits us,
the CI will be, uh, 2.5 to 3.0.

18:44.498 --> 18:48.377
The current trajectory makes it look
like Mokpo will be where it hits first.

18:48.460 --> 18:49.711
[Mi-jin] That's correct.

18:49.795 --> 18:54.007
If it does enter through Mokpo,
central pressure would be 970,

18:54.091 --> 18:58.178
and the maximum sustained wind
would be more than 30m per hour.

18:59.054 --> 19:01.223
With those measurements,
it would then be stronger

19:01.306 --> 19:03.642
than Prapiroon from 2018.

19:03.725 --> 19:06.895
AVERAGE DIFFERENCES
IN SEA SURFACE TEMPERATURES

19:06.979 --> 19:09.064
[sighs, clears throat]

19:09.148 --> 19:11.441
[suspenseful music]

19:11.525 --> 19:12.985
[sighs]

19:17.614 --> 19:19.867
[Bong-chan exhales heavily]

19:22.786 --> 19:23.912
[sighs]

19:25.706 --> 19:27.875
The 14th of the season, Typhoon Ricky,

19:27.958 --> 19:29.960
is headed north toward
the Korean peninsula.

19:30.043 --> 19:32.754
On our chart here,
the typhoon's eye looks rather vivid,

19:32.838 --> 19:34.339
which means it will be quite powerful.

19:34.423 --> 19:39.094
In the center of the typhoon is a gale,
as strong as 100km per hour.

19:40.971 --> 19:43.098
If the forecast predicts a typhoon…

19:43.182 --> 19:44.474
- Mom.
- Hm?

19:44.558 --> 19:47.019
Do you know how far we could go
at 100km an hour?

19:48.103 --> 19:49.313
I'm not…

19:49.897 --> 19:52.858
Seoul and Jeonju are about 200km away.

19:52.941 --> 19:56.028
So that means going a hundred,
we can get there in only two hours.

19:56.111 --> 19:57.321
Isn't the wind crazy?

19:57.404 --> 19:59.198
Wow. That's very interesting.

19:59.281 --> 20:01.575
I learned it on the trip to the KMA.

20:01.658 --> 20:04.119
[female reporter] Civilians are advised
to be on high alert. 

20:04.203 --> 20:06.413
Especially in areas with low visibility
or damage-prone.

20:06.496 --> 20:09.041
Those in farming areas
should avoid outdoor activities…

20:09.124 --> 20:11.960
It was pretty cool
going to see Dad at work.

20:12.044 --> 20:13.420
He's different in person.

20:15.130 --> 20:16.340
[sighs]

20:16.423 --> 20:19.760
You ate the ham, why?
You know you're allergic to it.

20:19.843 --> 20:21.220
I guess I might have forgot.

20:22.137 --> 20:23.764
You can never forget about that.

20:24.348 --> 20:27.142
Don't you remember going to the hospital
when you were younger?

20:27.226 --> 20:28.977
'Cause you had rice
with pork sausage in it.

20:31.063 --> 20:32.064
[Bo-mi] Hmm.

20:32.606 --> 20:33.523
I'm hungry.

20:34.107 --> 20:35.651
Do we have any snacks?

20:40.364 --> 20:41.823
You won't be able to visit again.

20:42.407 --> 20:44.618
It's the busiest time
of the year for the KMA.

20:46.036 --> 20:48.121
[dramatic music]

20:48.205 --> 20:51.041
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

20:52.376 --> 20:53.961
You should take your medication, too.

20:54.044 --> 20:55.754
It's right on the table if you look.

20:57.756 --> 20:59.633
- [Bo-mi] Mom.
- Hm?

21:01.718 --> 21:03.553
You're getting divorced?

21:07.349 --> 21:08.392
[gasps]

21:14.898 --> 21:16.483
Take your meds with your snack.

21:25.242 --> 21:27.577
[breathes sharply]

21:43.051 --> 21:44.303
How's your daughter doing?

21:45.137 --> 21:47.347
Oh, she's all right. She's back home.

21:49.349 --> 21:50.350
What a relief.

21:50.434 --> 21:52.352
It must have been stressful.

21:52.436 --> 21:55.188
It was. Her mom's taking care of her.

21:55.272 --> 21:56.815
[sucks teeth]

21:56.898 --> 21:59.985
I don't know what I've been doing
all this time.

22:01.111 --> 22:04.364
I thought it was good
to be such a hard worker, but…

22:05.407 --> 22:09.119
Looking back,
I was justifying being a lazy dad.

22:09.202 --> 22:13.123
Who doesn't know their kid's allergies?
I fed it to her.

22:14.374 --> 22:17.419
[sighs]
I put my own kid in the hospital.

22:22.132 --> 22:25.052
There are a million kinds
of dads out there.

22:25.927 --> 22:28.722
Having a dad
that's always available is great.

22:29.514 --> 22:32.350
There's a lot to be said for a dad
that works hard, though.

22:32.434 --> 22:33.727
I think it's equally great.

22:36.188 --> 22:37.355
Trying to make me feel better?

22:38.565 --> 22:39.941
If it's working.

22:40.025 --> 22:41.026
Yeah.

22:41.109 --> 22:44.488
[both chuckling]

22:44.571 --> 22:45.447
I'm all right.

22:46.198 --> 22:48.992
Gosh. Two typhoons are coming in
any day now.

22:49.076 --> 22:50.327
I need my head in the game.

22:50.911 --> 22:54.122
I know. And one could be stronger
than Prapiroon, lucky us.

22:54.206 --> 22:57.918
Also, I wanted to say,
I think you made a great call earlier.

22:58.794 --> 23:00.921
Sending Lee Si-woo out in the field.

23:02.714 --> 23:04.633
Thank you. It worked out, huh?

23:05.550 --> 23:07.552
[mellow music]

23:11.431 --> 23:13.433
- [Ki-jun] Thank you.
- [all] Goodbye.

23:13.517 --> 23:15.143
[Min-jun] Thank you. Thank you.

23:16.978 --> 23:18.105
[sighs]

23:20.023 --> 23:22.567
How many died from Typhoon Prapiroon?

23:22.651 --> 23:26.530
Thirty-eight deaths and missing.
Three hundred sixty-six injured.

23:26.613 --> 23:29.032
Oh. Was property damage that bad, too?

23:29.116 --> 23:32.577
Seventy billion for the capital.
Casualties are more important, though.

23:33.245 --> 23:35.747
Also, is something going on
with Miss Chae?

23:37.833 --> 23:39.501
I just haven't seen her in a while.

23:40.085 --> 23:43.171
Oh, she needed some time off.
I told her so.

23:44.297 --> 23:46.258
- [inhales sharply]
- Are you…

23:48.051 --> 23:49.094
Are we what?

23:49.761 --> 23:51.680
…gonna have a baby?

23:55.308 --> 23:56.184
- [sighs]
- [foot thumps]

23:56.268 --> 23:58.103
- Assistant Director Kim.
- Yes?

23:58.186 --> 24:01.022
Don't you have to tell the press
the briefing time?

24:01.106 --> 24:03.817
[gasps]
Oh, right. I'm so out of it.

24:09.030 --> 24:09.865
[sighs]

24:19.249 --> 24:21.585
[soft music]

24:31.094 --> 24:32.137
Dong-jin.

24:32.220 --> 24:33.305
[Dong-jin] Yu-jin!

24:34.264 --> 24:36.725
- [Yu-jin] Come here!
- I'm here!

24:36.808 --> 24:39.186
[grunts]
How have you been, big guy?

24:39.269 --> 24:40.812
What took you so long?

24:41.396 --> 24:44.065
- I missed you with my whole heart.
- Did you?

24:44.774 --> 24:47.277
- Oh, boy. You're growing, aren't you?
- Huh?

24:48.069 --> 24:50.906
- Here you are. Hey, welcome.
- [Yu-jin] Hey.

24:52.157 --> 24:53.325
Is his dad here?

24:53.408 --> 24:55.327
Oh, he's moving the boat
before the typhoon.

24:55.410 --> 24:56.870
- Come in.
- Mm.

24:58.205 --> 24:59.289
Let's go.

25:05.337 --> 25:09.132
JEJU OFFICE

25:11.176 --> 25:13.678
Check the AWS.
Make sure it's working before you go.

25:13.762 --> 25:14.679
Sure, I will.

25:15.931 --> 25:18.600
- You're tagging along?
- Since I'm gonna be here a while,

25:18.683 --> 25:20.936
I thought I should know
where they're stationed, don't you?

25:21.019 --> 25:23.939
Ah, you're a real weather guy, huh?
Don't work too late.

25:24.022 --> 25:25.899
- Yeah, thanks.
- [employee 1] Okay. Let's go.

25:33.782 --> 25:35.116
[Ha-kyung] What's going on?

25:35.200 --> 25:36.826
Why is it slowed down like that?

25:36.910 --> 25:39.996
They're figuring it out,
we're not sure why at this point in time.

25:40.830 --> 25:43.583
Been over the sea southwest of Jeju
for an hour now.

25:44.626 --> 25:46.670
What now, huh?

25:47.420 --> 25:50.757
The typhoon has stopped moving,
stuck over the Jeju sea.

25:50.840 --> 25:53.635
We're looking into the cause as we speak.

25:53.718 --> 25:55.553
Oh, no…

25:59.391 --> 26:02.352
[Mi-jin] It's currently 7 p.m.,
and Typhoon Ricky has suddenly turned

26:02.435 --> 26:03.645
towards the east.

26:03.728 --> 26:06.231
It's stagnant to the southwest.
I need an explanation.

26:06.940 --> 26:09.359
The upper and lower parts
could have separated

26:09.442 --> 26:11.403
and influenced its movement, right?

26:11.486 --> 26:12.737
It is a possibility.

26:12.821 --> 26:15.532
It's difficult to determine
with only satellite pictures.

26:17.993 --> 26:21.037
[Ha-kyung] I'd like to see
the current adiabatic chart in Jeju.

26:21.121 --> 26:22.831
Could your team do that?

26:22.914 --> 26:26.459
We have to do
a sonde observation from Seongsan.

26:26.543 --> 26:28.670
The observation vehicle
is in Seongsan now.

26:28.753 --> 26:32.799
Well, my team happens to have
our observation van in Seongsan currently.

26:33.383 --> 26:35.593
What do you think?
Should we do the sonde or not?

26:38.805 --> 26:41.141
You sure the adiabatic chart
will be enough for you?

26:41.725 --> 26:43.184
Yes. We just need to check

26:43.268 --> 26:45.687
the upper and lower parts
from about five kilometers above.

26:45.770 --> 26:47.772
[suspenseful music]

26:47.856 --> 26:48.773
[sighs]

26:51.109 --> 26:53.987
SPECIAL OBSERVATION VEHICLE

26:54.070 --> 26:57.407
[leaves rustling]

27:04.956 --> 27:07.292
[air hissing]

27:08.043 --> 27:08.918
[blows air]

27:12.339 --> 27:13.465
Excuse me.

27:13.548 --> 27:16.634
How many AWSs are on Jeju Island in total?

27:16.718 --> 27:17.969
Twenty-five altogether.

27:18.053 --> 27:19.220
Oh.

27:19.971 --> 27:21.723
Will we check all those today?

27:21.806 --> 27:24.309
Hey, the island is huge.
We'd never make it back.

27:24.392 --> 27:27.270
We're on a time crunch, so we're
only checking eight on the eastern side.

27:27.354 --> 27:28.772
[chuckles]
Okay.

27:30.607 --> 27:32.150
[Yu-jin humming]

27:33.026 --> 27:34.319
Let's go.

27:34.986 --> 27:36.529
Huh? Si-woo, oppa?

27:38.823 --> 27:40.367
Oh, what brings you to Jeju?

27:40.450 --> 27:43.620
[Yu-jin] Uh, I'm visiting my mom
and step-family.

27:44.287 --> 27:45.121
[Si-woo] Oh.

27:45.205 --> 27:47.540
This is my mom and my brother.

27:47.624 --> 27:49.250
Oh, hello.

27:50.085 --> 27:52.003
- Hi.
- What brings you out here?

27:52.087 --> 27:54.214
Oh, the typhoon center is out here.

27:54.297 --> 27:55.382
[Dong-jin] Oh, hey.

27:55.465 --> 27:57.467
- You work at the KMA, don't you?
- [Si-woo] Mm-hm.

27:58.051 --> 27:59.219
I do, and it's great.

27:59.803 --> 28:02.097
Are you my sister's boyfriend?

28:02.180 --> 28:03.681
- Uh…
- [Yu-jin's mom] Goodness.

28:03.765 --> 28:05.809
What are you talking about? She's married.

28:05.892 --> 28:08.353
You've met your brother-in-law.
[chuckles]

28:08.436 --> 28:09.938
Oh, yeah, that guy.

28:12.482 --> 28:15.068
[employee 1] Mr. Lee,
Director Sung just called.

28:15.151 --> 28:17.654
They want a sonde observation
in Seongsan right now.

28:17.737 --> 28:18.947
Oh, uh, right now?

28:19.030 --> 28:22.033
Yeah. It sounds like the typhoon
isn't doing what we thought it was.

28:22.117 --> 28:23.910
- Oh--
- Oh, can I come, too?

28:24.411 --> 28:25.954
[Yu-jin's mom] Oh, no, Dong-jin.

28:26.037 --> 28:27.163
[chuckling]

28:28.206 --> 28:30.708
[Dong-jin] Please? Can I go with you?

28:30.792 --> 28:32.794
Yu-jin, can I go with him?

28:32.877 --> 28:34.587
Calm down. They've got work to do.

28:34.671 --> 28:37.841
It'd be so cool, please? Please.

28:37.924 --> 28:39.175
[Dong-jin] I'll be good.

28:39.259 --> 28:41.469
Uh, would it be all right
if they tag along?

28:41.553 --> 28:43.096
They could watch from the car.

28:43.179 --> 28:45.807
[playful music]

28:48.893 --> 28:51.354
[chuckles]
Can they go?

28:59.946 --> 29:01.322
[line rings]

29:01.406 --> 29:04.367
- [Mrs. Bae] What do you want?
- There's a typhoon coming in.

29:04.451 --> 29:06.369
Took you long enough to call.

29:06.453 --> 29:08.121
On the news, they kept saying that

29:08.204 --> 29:11.374
a typhoon's coming
and we better prepare for a big one.

29:13.042 --> 29:14.919
Okay, then. That was all.

29:15.003 --> 29:18.298
[Mrs. Bae] Hey, hey. You're just
hanging up without asking about me?

29:18.381 --> 29:20.049
Why? Do you have something to say?

29:21.342 --> 29:22.177
[grunts]

29:22.886 --> 29:24.220
That man that works for you.

29:24.804 --> 29:26.514
If it's about Assistant Shin,
I'm hanging up.

29:26.598 --> 29:29.559
Oh, no. Oh, no. I don't mean that one.

29:29.642 --> 29:32.604
You know, the one that looks young
that I met in the elevator,

29:32.687 --> 29:34.105
the guy that's staying with you.

29:34.189 --> 29:35.732
Was his name Lee Si-woo? Uh…

29:36.524 --> 29:37.650
What about him?

29:39.110 --> 29:40.403
Did he say anything?

29:40.987 --> 29:42.447
Lee Si-woo? Why would he?

29:42.530 --> 29:45.116
Did-- Some-- What are you talking about?

29:45.200 --> 29:47.577
I got dinner with him. Why?

29:47.660 --> 29:50.455
Oh, Mom, you got dinner with him?
When was that--

29:50.538 --> 29:51.748
I mean… Why?

29:51.831 --> 29:53.666
That's inappropriate and it's weird.

29:53.750 --> 29:56.377
What was I supposed to do,
you wouldn't answer your phone,

29:56.461 --> 29:58.505
and I had to know about the guy above you.

29:58.588 --> 30:01.549
Oh, Mom, did you talk to Si-woo
about Assistant Shin and me?

30:01.633 --> 30:04.594
Shame on you. Shame on you
for not picking up my call.

30:04.677 --> 30:06.846
You should've learned by now, huh?

30:07.430 --> 30:09.307
I had to do something.
You wouldn't answer.

30:09.891 --> 30:12.393
Well, it… it's still really wrong!

30:12.477 --> 30:15.188
How is it wrong? What's wrong about it?

30:15.271 --> 30:17.148
His director's mother treated him
to a dinner.

30:17.232 --> 30:19.150
Why are you acting like it's illegal?

30:21.277 --> 30:22.111
[sighs]

30:23.404 --> 30:25.490
It's not how it was a long time ago, Mom.

30:25.573 --> 30:28.493
It's bad enough you met
my subordinate in private,

30:28.576 --> 30:30.411
but you asked questions about me, too?

30:31.162 --> 30:33.748
If you do it again,
and I'll never see you again, ever.

30:33.832 --> 30:37.210
Ugh. No, you're so dramatic. Calm down.

30:38.586 --> 30:39.587
Hey.

30:41.005 --> 30:44.050
Have you noticed how he is?

30:44.133 --> 30:45.301
What?

30:45.885 --> 30:48.555
I-- I think the Lee guy
has feelings for you.

30:49.472 --> 30:51.474
[quirky music]

30:52.934 --> 30:55.061
The way he talks about you,
I think he has…

30:55.144 --> 30:57.480
What's the word for it?
Uh, it's something like…

30:57.564 --> 30:58.940
Um, wait, a mush.

30:59.023 --> 31:02.277
No, a crush. He has a crush on you.

31:04.153 --> 31:07.156
- [line beeps]
- You still there? Hey, did you…

31:07.240 --> 31:08.867
Hey, Ha-kyung, did you…

31:10.660 --> 31:12.370
[sighs]
She won't let it go.

31:13.329 --> 31:15.999
[cell phone buzzing]

31:16.082 --> 31:17.667
MOM

31:22.922 --> 31:24.299
Well, that was odd.

31:24.799 --> 31:27.552
Maybe she likes him, too?

31:28.553 --> 31:31.264
Eh, there's no way.

31:31.848 --> 31:34.809
Tae-kyung would, but Ha-kyung would never.

31:34.893 --> 31:37.228
He's way too high risk,
she always wants someone that's safe.

31:49.949 --> 31:51.367
[automated voice] Doors opening.

32:00.627 --> 32:01.794
Doors closing.

32:04.380 --> 32:06.633
- Leaving?
- Mm-hm.

32:07.884 --> 32:10.678
- You're not, though?
- Mm-mm, just getting dinner.

32:11.179 --> 32:12.305
Mm.

32:19.646 --> 32:20.939
Could I eat with you?

32:24.901 --> 32:26.903
[gloomy music]

32:40.750 --> 32:43.670
- [employee 1] The wind's picking up.
- Yeah, it is.

32:45.004 --> 32:46.965
DATE OF DATA
JULY 30, 2022

32:48.424 --> 32:49.592
I got it.

32:55.807 --> 32:57.600
You have to let it go and call.

32:58.226 --> 33:01.437
- What are you saying?
- You want Ki-jun to call first, don't you?

33:01.521 --> 33:02.814
How did you know?

33:02.897 --> 33:05.483
It's obvious. A mother knows these things.

33:07.819 --> 33:11.239
Don't drag this out,
not when you're married.

33:11.990 --> 33:16.536
It's best if you call today,
say you'll let it go, and go back.

33:17.161 --> 33:19.622
Oh, Mom. I just got here.

33:19.706 --> 33:22.417
You can visit any time.
Come on the holidays.

33:24.293 --> 33:25.628
Why?

33:25.712 --> 33:29.298
You're worried that I'll mess up
my first marriage like you did?

33:29.382 --> 33:31.551
[sentimental music]

33:31.634 --> 33:32.760
Mm-hm.

33:34.012 --> 33:35.054
That's right.

33:36.347 --> 33:40.101
I got married when I was too young,
I really didn't know.

33:41.102 --> 33:43.771
The pettiness only made things worse.

33:44.355 --> 33:46.441
Okay, let's move on.

33:49.318 --> 33:52.530
I know Ki-jun is a good man.
See, mothers know.

33:53.948 --> 33:57.577
I don't know what you're fighting about,
you have to let it go, hm?

33:58.828 --> 34:01.122
Oh, baby, you know that.

34:02.331 --> 34:05.126
[sighs]
I can take care of it. Thanks.

34:05.877 --> 34:06.794
Drop it.

34:15.470 --> 34:16.345
You want a drink?

34:17.180 --> 34:19.223
I have to go back after this.

34:19.307 --> 34:20.933
Two typhoons are coming in soon.

34:26.314 --> 34:27.940
[indistinct chatter]

34:28.983 --> 34:30.526
[breathes deeply]

34:33.029 --> 34:35.156
Was I so frustrating
you couldn't stand it, Ha-kyung?

34:37.909 --> 34:41.621
Am I just an untrustworthy idiot
and a total loser?

34:44.707 --> 34:46.125
I could ask the same to you.

34:47.585 --> 34:51.255
Was I so work-obsessed, insensitive,
that I made you fall out of love?

34:52.757 --> 34:53.883
I mean…

34:53.966 --> 34:56.344
I can't really say you weren't.

34:56.427 --> 34:58.346
Honestly, with some distance, though,

34:58.429 --> 35:00.515
you're great
and anyone's lucky to have you.

35:01.474 --> 35:02.809
You're smart,

35:02.892 --> 35:05.269
and responsible,
and you're really good at keeping calm.

35:06.062 --> 35:11.692
And also, if I wasn't competing with work,
you were really compassionate and kind.

35:11.776 --> 35:16.239
I think we just weren't the right match
for each other.

35:17.657 --> 35:18.783
You're okay.

35:19.450 --> 35:21.911
You go all-in at work,
even with things you've never done.

35:21.994 --> 35:24.038
You have courage and it shows.

35:24.997 --> 35:28.459
I will say you did some things
that were tough to work through.

35:28.543 --> 35:29.377
[chuckles softly]

35:29.877 --> 35:31.129
But you're not awful.

35:33.923 --> 35:36.592
You're not the right one for me.

35:36.676 --> 35:38.761
[tender music]

35:41.139 --> 35:44.058
I didn't know you saw me in that way.

35:45.226 --> 35:46.435
And honestly,

35:46.519 --> 35:50.565
I thought you looked down on me
the whole relationship.

35:50.648 --> 35:52.817
"Oh God, what an idiot."

35:52.900 --> 35:55.319
"How did he make it this far?"
That sort of thing.

35:56.863 --> 35:58.823
I wanted your best at what you do.

35:58.906 --> 36:00.533
I know you're good at your work.

36:05.621 --> 36:07.832
We should've said all this sooner, huh?

36:10.877 --> 36:13.629
Maybe we didn't realize
we had to say it out loud.

36:14.255 --> 36:15.798
But I wouldn't have known.

36:16.632 --> 36:17.925
I misunderstood you

36:18.926 --> 36:20.136
and got resentful.

36:20.720 --> 36:21.804
You did.

36:22.430 --> 36:26.475
There are so many things we wouldn't know
unless we express ourselves.

36:29.729 --> 36:30.771
[Ha-kyung] It's true.

36:30.855 --> 36:33.733
There are so many things we wouldn't know
unless we share them.

36:36.152 --> 36:41.032
So why did we expect each other
to know these without saying anything?

36:42.450 --> 36:44.952
[raindrops pattering]

36:48.414 --> 36:50.041
Oh? That's rain.

36:50.124 --> 36:51.918
Mr. Lee, I'll be right back.

36:52.001 --> 36:52.960
Okay.

37:09.268 --> 37:15.691
[air hissing]

37:23.991 --> 37:25.993
[somber music]

37:42.802 --> 37:44.262
[cell phone buzzes]

37:47.556 --> 37:48.557
[Ki-jun] Where are you?

37:48.641 --> 37:50.685
At least tell me where you're staying.

38:01.946 --> 38:03.155
[sighs]

38:12.581 --> 38:14.292
[air hissing]

38:22.466 --> 38:25.177
[muffled hissing]

38:29.265 --> 38:31.142
[explosion]

38:31.225 --> 38:33.227
[suspenseful music]

38:40.401 --> 38:41.569
[mouthing]
Si-woo…

38:45.948 --> 38:46.866
Si-woo, oppa!

38:49.410 --> 38:50.494
[Yu-jin] Si-woo!

38:51.412 --> 38:53.581
- Si-woo, can you hear me?
- [employee 1] Mr. Lee!

38:53.664 --> 38:55.249
[Yu-jin] Don't move too much.

38:55.333 --> 38:57.543
[groaning]

38:57.626 --> 38:58.878
Stay with us, Mr. Lee.

39:04.759 --> 39:06.927
We can't just ignore it.

39:07.011 --> 39:10.222
PRESENT

39:11.098 --> 39:13.184
Can you check in with the hospital again?

39:13.267 --> 39:14.226
Huh?

39:14.310 --> 39:16.354
If there's news about Lee Si-woo,

39:16.437 --> 39:18.397
- I'd like to know.
- Oh, okay.

39:19.690 --> 39:22.068
[phone keys clicking]

39:25.821 --> 39:28.657
Going on with the last update
we heard from Jeju,

39:28.741 --> 39:31.494
he, thankfully,
isn't in critical condition currently.

39:32.953 --> 39:33.996
So you…

39:35.456 --> 39:37.458
- Huh?
- [Myung-han] You're saying…

39:38.042 --> 39:40.419
you're not gonna compensate him
for his injury,

39:40.503 --> 39:43.589
because it's not critical enough,
is that it?

39:44.298 --> 39:45.674
[Bong-chan chuckles softly]
No, sir.

39:46.217 --> 39:48.928
We'll make sure he's taken care of,
financially and otherwise.

39:49.553 --> 39:51.555
I said that only
because I thought you want to know

39:51.639 --> 39:54.934
- how your son's doing in the hospital.
- You're trying to avoid things.

39:55.851 --> 39:57.686
This isn't my first rodeo.

39:57.770 --> 40:02.400
I know you're doing damage control,
'cause you cheapskates are all the same.

40:02.483 --> 40:03.609
You don't wanna pay out!

40:03.692 --> 40:05.361
It's not gonna work on us!

40:05.861 --> 40:09.156
I think, Mr. Lee,
that you're way out of line.

40:09.240 --> 40:10.324
I don't want to hear it!

40:11.409 --> 40:13.953
So we should cut to the chase,

40:14.036 --> 40:16.580
and decide the amount,
then we'll go our separate ways!

40:17.456 --> 40:18.666
Okay, listen.

40:18.749 --> 40:19.917
[knocks on door]

40:21.419 --> 40:22.461
Yeah?

40:24.130 --> 40:24.964
What is it?

40:25.047 --> 40:27.967
I got off the phone
with the hospital just now.

40:28.050 --> 40:29.969
They transferred him to the general ward.

40:30.052 --> 40:32.263
- His eyes were slightly injured.
- He…

40:33.097 --> 40:34.890
hurt his eyes?

40:36.267 --> 40:37.393
- Oh.
- [Myung-han] Well, then…

40:39.812 --> 40:43.149
That bad of an injury counts
for disability level one, yeah?

40:43.899 --> 40:45.568
- [sighs]
- He could still fully recover.

40:45.651 --> 40:47.278
It's not a guaranteed disability,
you know?

40:47.361 --> 40:49.363
I know what it's like to be a dad
worried about his kid,

40:49.447 --> 40:51.615
- but you're going overboard.
- You're gonna judge me?

40:51.699 --> 40:53.701
What you guys are saying is too much!

40:54.368 --> 40:55.953
You're responsible! Without you, idiots,

40:56.036 --> 40:57.663
he wouldn't be laying in a hospital bed.

40:57.746 --> 41:00.708
So, I'm here for accountability,
'cause you hurt my boy!

41:00.791 --> 41:02.710
You're gonna fix his eyes?

41:04.295 --> 41:06.088
You're right. I'm sorry, Mr. Lee.

41:06.172 --> 41:07.173
That's right.

41:07.798 --> 41:09.967
Director Lady understands.

41:10.050 --> 41:12.928
So how about we go to Jeju together?

41:14.680 --> 41:15.723
What?

41:16.307 --> 41:19.477
You're so worried about how he is,
we should go and see for ourselves.

41:19.560 --> 41:21.729
Then we'll know
how this discussion should go.

41:28.861 --> 41:29.695
Director Jin.

41:29.778 --> 41:32.740
I heard what you said about him earlier.
He's your only son.

41:33.532 --> 41:34.492
Yeah.

41:35.367 --> 41:38.662
I've gotta take care of him
with this compensation.

41:38.746 --> 41:41.123
- Just for his sake, we gotta figure this--
- That's step two.

41:41.207 --> 41:44.084
First, you should go
and see how he is, if he's okay.

41:45.461 --> 41:48.797
We can't determine any compensation
until we've assessed things ourselves.

41:52.343 --> 41:54.512
We'll take the first flight out tomorrow.

41:54.595 --> 41:56.096
Is that all right, sir?

41:56.180 --> 41:59.016
Yeah. Of course. Get your tickets.

41:59.099 --> 42:00.684
You can handle it on your own?

42:01.310 --> 42:02.436
Yes, I can.

42:03.479 --> 42:05.064
See you at the airport early tomorrow.

42:05.147 --> 42:07.358
[pensive music]

42:17.785 --> 42:18.786
[sighs]

42:18.869 --> 42:19.912
Huh?

42:21.080 --> 42:22.873
Why do you need to tag along?

42:22.957 --> 42:26.418
If they need extra help,
they should get someone from HR.

42:26.502 --> 42:28.462
I have some urgent business out there.

42:29.046 --> 42:30.005
I can't.

42:30.089 --> 42:32.591
There are two major typhoons
coming any day now.

42:33.217 --> 42:34.802
You won't let me go?

42:35.594 --> 42:37.555
Mm-mm. No way.

42:39.014 --> 42:41.976
Then I have to take a leave of absence.

42:42.643 --> 42:44.478
- You what?
- The typhoons?

42:45.187 --> 42:47.982
Yeah, it's important,
and we have to keep everyone safe.

42:48.065 --> 42:51.485
But, you know, I've never taken
a day off in typhoon season.

42:51.569 --> 42:53.362
Not since I began here.

42:53.445 --> 42:55.072
Even when I needed to.

42:55.573 --> 42:56.991
Not a half-day, not a long lunch.

42:57.074 --> 42:59.201
Every year, I give everything to this job.

42:59.285 --> 43:00.619
Yeah, and your co-workers do, too.

43:00.703 --> 43:01.787
[Ki-jun] That's my point.

43:01.870 --> 43:04.206
Everyone here works like I do,
then they'll be able

43:04.290 --> 43:05.749
to cover me for a day.

43:06.542 --> 43:09.044
I'll ask you again,
can I take the time off?

43:09.128 --> 43:11.422
Oh, why can't you do this another season?

43:11.505 --> 43:12.631
I wish I could.

43:13.591 --> 43:15.718
Except Yu-jin left me now, so I…

43:18.304 --> 43:19.138
Huh?

43:19.722 --> 43:21.098
[Ju-won] Is that why?

43:21.181 --> 43:23.559
That's why she hasn't been attending
any of the briefings?

43:26.353 --> 43:30.149
Our whole life together
could fall apart in pieces.

43:30.232 --> 43:31.108
[gasps]

43:32.192 --> 43:33.527
Can you let me go?

43:34.445 --> 43:36.530
[sighs]

43:39.575 --> 43:41.577
[mellow music]

43:43.454 --> 43:44.788
[line rings]

43:44.872 --> 43:46.040
Director Jin.

43:46.874 --> 43:50.377
Is there a way you could take me
to Jeju Island?

43:53.213 --> 43:54.340
Oh.

43:56.050 --> 43:58.052
[mellow music]

43:59.219 --> 44:00.220
[sighs]

44:10.898 --> 44:13.067
[plane zooming]

44:21.367 --> 44:23.619
[mellow music continues]

44:33.629 --> 44:35.923
[Myung-han snoring]

44:42.513 --> 44:43.972
[Dong-han sighs]

44:50.646 --> 44:51.772
[sniffs]
Hm?

44:53.774 --> 44:55.067
Another all-nighter?

44:55.150 --> 44:56.568
Yeah.

44:56.652 --> 44:58.862
Why… Why are you here so early?

44:59.446 --> 45:01.073
I needed to talk with you.

45:07.329 --> 45:08.414
[Mrs. Bae sighs]

45:09.915 --> 45:11.959
[Mrs. Bae] Tae-kyung, breakfast is ready.

45:13.710 --> 45:15.045
That girl.

45:15.129 --> 45:17.256
Tae-kyung, come out and eat.

45:22.678 --> 45:23.720
Hm?

45:24.221 --> 45:26.098
She's never out this early.

45:27.558 --> 45:29.685
[soft music playing]

45:36.233 --> 45:37.443
Ah.

45:48.996 --> 45:49.872
[sighs]

45:50.497 --> 45:52.833
You must be tired from working all night.

45:52.916 --> 45:55.043
You could have called
and rescheduled for later.

45:55.919 --> 45:58.130
Aren't you supposed
to sign this contract by noon?

45:58.213 --> 46:01.341
Yeah, but it's not really
a huge deal at all.

46:01.425 --> 46:03.302
[sucks teeth]
So…

46:04.595 --> 46:07.598
I looked over the contract a few times

46:07.681 --> 46:09.933
- and something stood out.
- Hm?

46:11.477 --> 46:14.354
Right here, the "exclusive publication."

46:14.438 --> 46:15.898
What does this mean, exactly?

46:17.232 --> 46:19.067
Oh, I don't really know.

46:20.569 --> 46:24.281
What about all these restrictions
on royalties?

46:24.364 --> 46:28.869
Uh, that's just saying how much I get
when each book gets sold in stores.

46:29.912 --> 46:33.624
Then shouldn't Article 11 leave you
with franchise rights?

46:37.544 --> 46:40.339
Why, should I ask for that?

46:40.422 --> 46:42.841
[quirky music]

46:42.925 --> 46:44.051
Yeah, uh…

46:44.718 --> 46:47.054
Can I talk to whoever sent you this thing?

46:47.137 --> 46:48.472
What?

46:55.395 --> 46:56.730
[line ringing]

46:56.813 --> 46:59.107
Hello, it's Jin Tae-kyung.
Someone wants to talk…

46:59.191 --> 47:01.777
Oh, here he is. Here.

47:01.860 --> 47:02.819
Thanks.

47:04.488 --> 47:05.572
Yes, hello?

47:05.656 --> 47:09.535
Well, I have some questions
about the contract.

47:09.618 --> 47:12.079
Starting with Article 11, that won't do.

47:12.829 --> 47:16.917
Also, we need a fair percentage
on royalties, understand me?

47:17.834 --> 47:19.878
She's the illustrator
and the author of everything.

47:19.962 --> 47:21.630
You just print it for her.

47:21.713 --> 47:22.631
Who am I?

47:24.967 --> 47:26.760
Well, I'm her manager, obviously.

47:28.887 --> 47:29.930
Yes.

47:31.431 --> 47:32.808
That's all right, and please,

47:32.891 --> 47:34.935
give us a call back
when it's been worked out.

47:35.018 --> 47:35.894
Great.

47:35.978 --> 47:37.980
["Melting" by CHEEZE playing]

47:38.063 --> 47:41.692
They're gonna adjust the percentage
for your royalties.

47:41.775 --> 47:43.318
They'll get back to you soon.

47:43.402 --> 47:44.861
I see.

47:44.945 --> 47:47.739
You have to ask them questions.

47:47.823 --> 47:50.325
Make sure you understand
and have a fair deal,

47:50.409 --> 47:52.244
or they'll pull a fast one on you.

47:53.120 --> 47:55.622
You could lose your rights
to your characters and more

47:55.706 --> 47:57.374
on top of them for the royalties.

47:57.457 --> 48:00.294
You have to be careful
with anything they give you, okay?

48:00.377 --> 48:01.920
I've been divorced before.

48:04.381 --> 48:05.257
And?

48:06.508 --> 48:08.927
What? Oh.
[nervous chuckle]

48:09.011 --> 48:10.887
I thought you should know.

48:15.851 --> 48:19.855
There's a myth about penguins
that everyone thinks it's true.

48:19.938 --> 48:21.064
What is it?

48:21.148 --> 48:22.816
That they mate for life.

48:23.734 --> 48:24.735
That's not true?

48:25.527 --> 48:28.572
There was a documentary
where this penguin couple

48:28.655 --> 48:30.866
worked together to raise their chick.

48:30.949 --> 48:32.451
That was breeding season.

48:33.035 --> 48:35.454
The next year, if it wasn't a good match,

48:35.537 --> 48:37.289
they're free to find
a new partner to be with.

48:38.707 --> 48:39.666
But why…

48:40.500 --> 48:43.670
are you telling me about this now?

48:45.255 --> 48:48.050
'Cause animals don't care
if anyone's had a mate before.

48:48.133 --> 48:50.135
[bright music]

48:54.806 --> 48:56.850
Would you eat breakfast with me?

48:57.434 --> 48:58.310
Yeah.

48:58.393 --> 48:59.686
[chuckles]

49:10.530 --> 49:12.908
Well, I'll listen. But you should eat.

49:21.458 --> 49:22.668
What is this?

49:24.002 --> 49:25.170
[sniffles]

49:26.588 --> 49:28.006
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

49:28.090 --> 49:29.716
Look it over and sign it.

49:29.800 --> 49:31.885
[somber music]

49:34.596 --> 49:36.848
[breathes deeply]

49:36.932 --> 49:39.643
- Sweetheart, this--
- Don't think this was a sudden decision.

49:40.227 --> 49:41.436
It was a long time coming.

49:41.520 --> 49:44.147
I hope you respect that this is my choice.

49:54.908 --> 49:57.744
I'm so sorry, Hyang-rae.

49:58.453 --> 50:01.832
I made you raise Bo-mi
all on your own and…

50:02.332 --> 50:05.752
You must have felt so alone
while I was gone.

50:05.836 --> 50:07.421
And truly, I apologize.

50:08.422 --> 50:09.673
[Dong-han sighs]

50:09.756 --> 50:10.966
It's just…

50:13.176 --> 50:14.720
I never would've chosen to leave you.

50:14.803 --> 50:17.639
- It was always for work.
- No more excuses.

50:18.223 --> 50:21.977
And at first, you had no say,
it had to be either Busan or Namhae.

50:22.060 --> 50:24.896
Neither one was home for us.
Either way, you'd be leaving.

50:24.980 --> 50:27.816
But over time,
I realized you like being gone.

50:30.569 --> 50:31.528
Hmm.

50:31.611 --> 50:34.364
You're right. I did.

50:35.490 --> 50:38.243
- And she got to you.
- Who got to who?

50:38.326 --> 50:40.871
The TV woman that speaks for the KMA.

50:40.954 --> 50:43.498
- Jin Ha-kyung.
- Director Jin? What?

50:43.582 --> 50:45.417
What? What?

50:45.500 --> 50:46.877
I saw it.

50:47.586 --> 50:49.629
You were leaving the KMA together.

50:52.048 --> 50:54.176
[somber music]

51:03.018 --> 51:05.228
What? No! It's not…

51:05.729 --> 51:08.356
You're totally misunderstanding.
It wasn't that.

51:11.985 --> 51:13.195
It was work.

51:14.154 --> 51:15.572
Ask anyone.

51:15.655 --> 51:17.407
And it wasn't just me staying there.

51:17.491 --> 51:20.076
There was another forecaster,
Si-woo there, too.

51:20.160 --> 51:22.662
She was being nice
by letting us stay there

51:22.746 --> 51:23.747
instead of at the office.

51:25.415 --> 51:26.958
It's really not what you think.

51:27.042 --> 51:29.503
A-- Ask Si-woo.
He'll tell you exactly the same thing.

51:29.586 --> 51:32.130
And I swear on Bo-mi.
I swear it's really true.

51:32.714 --> 51:34.925
You're not really bringing Bo-mi
into this, are you?

51:35.842 --> 51:37.260
Right, I'm not.

51:38.011 --> 51:39.971
But I… I'd never do that.

51:40.055 --> 51:42.641
You know me,
it's insane that you'd think that at all.

51:45.769 --> 51:48.021
It is. And that's what I thought, too.

51:49.105 --> 51:51.107
In all that time,
it never crossed my mind.

51:51.191 --> 51:53.235
"Maybe he's cheating,
or has another family."

51:53.318 --> 51:54.986
Because I trusted you.

51:55.737 --> 51:57.614
So when I finally caught you…

51:58.907 --> 52:00.659
it hurt beyond words.

52:01.409 --> 52:03.495
Okay, Hyang-rae. I…

52:05.622 --> 52:08.333
How long did you actually stay with us
after you transferred?

52:08.959 --> 52:12.671
It seemed best for everyone,
you and Bo-mi, if I left and stayed away.

52:15.048 --> 52:17.008
No excuses, Dong-han.

52:17.092 --> 52:20.095
You chose to run away because
you couldn't face that we're hurting.

52:20.178 --> 52:21.429
Don't blame us for that.

52:22.639 --> 52:25.100
Do you have any idea
how much it hurt us that you left again?

52:28.395 --> 52:32.190
It was childish of me.

52:34.943 --> 52:35.861
[sniffs]

52:39.281 --> 52:41.324
Why do you make me feel so miserable?

52:43.451 --> 52:45.453
What did I do
to make you hate me like this?

52:45.537 --> 52:47.539
[somber music]

52:50.834 --> 52:52.377
I apologize.

52:53.086 --> 52:54.212
Hyang-rae.

52:54.713 --> 52:56.256
I'll come home and make it right.

52:56.339 --> 52:58.300
You think that's still an option?

52:58.383 --> 53:00.176
Please, one more chance.

53:00.260 --> 53:02.262
No, no more. Enough.

53:03.054 --> 53:04.973
Just be a decent man for once and sign it.

53:05.056 --> 53:05.932
Sign the paper

53:06.016 --> 53:08.685
and we can both go
and move on with our lives.

53:09.394 --> 53:11.688
It's what's best for everyone, hm?

53:18.945 --> 53:20.947
[somber music]

53:47.223 --> 53:51.186
[waves crashing]

53:51.269 --> 53:53.688
[raindrops pattering]

54:19.839 --> 54:21.883
[receptionist] What's the patient's
full name?

54:21.967 --> 54:22.801
Lee Si-woo.

54:22.884 --> 54:25.470
And who is Lee Si-woo to each of you?

54:25.553 --> 54:29.808
Uh, I'm his dad. Lee Si-woo's my son.

54:29.891 --> 54:31.977
My only kid. I'm his guardian.

54:33.144 --> 54:35.730
Over there to the right. He's Room 305.

54:35.814 --> 54:36.982
Thank you, miss.

54:37.065 --> 54:38.274
[Myung-han] Also…

54:46.616 --> 54:48.618
[somber music]

55:05.218 --> 55:07.220
["I Love You This Much" by Punch playing]

55:32.245 --> 55:33.413
Are you okay?

55:40.295 --> 55:43.506
[sobbing]

55:58.980 --> 56:00.190
I'm better now.

56:07.363 --> 56:08.364
No tears.

56:24.172 --> 56:25.548
[door opens]

56:26.216 --> 56:27.550
[Myung-han] Hey, Si-woo.

56:28.968 --> 56:31.304
What's wrong with you, huh?

56:31.888 --> 56:33.473
What's on your face?

56:33.556 --> 56:35.475
Tell me everything. What did they do?

56:36.768 --> 56:37.894
Dad, is that you?

56:37.977 --> 56:39.938
Yes. It's me. I'm here. I'll fix it.

56:40.021 --> 56:41.981
[Myung-han] Oh, God. Look at you.

56:42.065 --> 56:45.360
He's way worse than I thought he was.

56:47.028 --> 56:49.405
How did you get here? Uh, no.

56:49.489 --> 56:51.282
- Why are you here?
- [Myung-han] Come on, kid.

56:51.366 --> 56:53.952
What dad wouldn't come
when his only son gets hurt?

56:54.035 --> 56:57.163
I've been calling and calling you.
You wouldn't pick up, though.

56:57.247 --> 56:59.999
I was going crazy,
so I hit up the guys at your work.

57:00.083 --> 57:03.211
- You went to Headquarters?
- Hey, don't you worry, though.

57:03.294 --> 57:05.713
I went in and talked
to the head director guy.

57:05.797 --> 57:09.342
He knows he better get you
what he owes you, or else, believe me…

57:09.425 --> 57:11.803
I got it all under control, okay, kid?

57:12.470 --> 57:17.725
Oh, and it's just your eyes?
Did they check the rest of you, huh?

57:17.809 --> 57:20.270
- I'll do it. Let me look.
- [grunts]

57:20.770 --> 57:24.149
Hey, you got to tell me
where else you're hurt.

57:24.232 --> 57:26.776
We've got to milk 'em
for everything that we can.

57:26.860 --> 57:27.861
Got it?

57:29.696 --> 57:32.240
- Director Jin.
- Huh?

57:32.323 --> 57:33.700
Get this man out, please.

57:34.617 --> 57:35.743
[Myung-han] Huh?

57:37.662 --> 57:39.330
- Si-woo.
- I want you out.

57:39.414 --> 57:42.000
You should leave.
Seoul is missing you, I'm sure.

57:43.209 --> 57:45.336
[scoffs]
Are you kidding?

57:45.420 --> 57:48.173
I'm gonna be at your side
every second, don't worry.

57:48.256 --> 57:50.175
I want you to leave me alone!

57:52.802 --> 57:54.345
[breathes shakily]

57:54.429 --> 57:57.056
You don't know what you're saying.
How's your head?

57:57.140 --> 58:00.226
- How's your legs?
- Hi. I heard the guardian was present.

58:00.310 --> 58:03.605
Yeah, yeah, yeah, that's me.
Lee Si-woo means everything to me.

58:03.688 --> 58:06.691
Yes, good to meet you.
May I please have a word with you outside?

58:06.774 --> 58:08.193
Uh-huh. Yeah.

58:08.902 --> 58:09.736
[sobs]

58:10.445 --> 58:12.155
- Let's go.
- Okay.

58:12.238 --> 58:14.449
[door opens]

58:21.372 --> 58:22.332
He's just…

58:23.958 --> 58:26.544
acting out,
'cause he's so worried about you.

58:27.712 --> 58:29.380
He's not capable of that.

58:30.507 --> 58:32.008
He doesn't care that I'm injured.

58:32.634 --> 58:36.137
There's only one thing he came for,
and it has nothing to do with his son.

58:36.721 --> 58:39.182
- Si-woo--
- That's just the kind of bad father he is!

58:40.725 --> 58:43.520
You should not have brought him here!
Do you get it now?

58:46.481 --> 58:47.732
[exhales deeply]

58:52.904 --> 58:54.405
[sobbing]

59:02.288 --> 59:03.289
[sighs]

59:03.373 --> 59:06.000
Oh, what did I think coming here would do?

59:06.084 --> 59:08.878
Oh, I'm such an idiot.
[sighs]

59:10.713 --> 59:13.633
[doctor] He's been burned
on his face and neck.

59:15.093 --> 59:16.511
Thankfully, it's not severe.

59:16.594 --> 59:18.346
He won't need any kind of surgery,

59:18.429 --> 59:20.473
and I expect
he'll recover without scaring.

59:20.557 --> 59:22.684
What we're most concerned about
is possible injury

59:22.767 --> 59:24.269
to his left cornea from the explosion.

59:24.352 --> 59:26.980
We've done what we can
and only time will tell.

59:27.564 --> 59:29.065
[Myung-han] His cornea got hit?

59:30.108 --> 59:33.987
That means he could lose
his eyesight, couldn't he, right?

59:34.070 --> 59:37.365
He responded well to the treatment,
so, well, it's not likely we'll--

59:37.448 --> 59:38.741
I don't care about that stuff.

59:38.825 --> 59:39.701
[inhales sharply]

59:40.493 --> 59:43.538
"The explosion damaged
his cornea severely."

59:44.038 --> 59:47.500
Could you tell them that?
Could you say that exactly in your report?

59:48.918 --> 59:52.463
My son should get
everything he's entitled to.

59:52.547 --> 59:55.800
What you say in that report is gonna,
it'll make or break us.

59:57.260 --> 59:59.596
Do you get what I need you to do?

01:00:00.930 --> 01:00:02.181
[doctor] Well, I, uh…

01:00:03.933 --> 01:00:06.311
[rain pattering]

01:00:11.941 --> 01:00:13.943
[somber music]

01:00:31.669 --> 01:00:33.504
You should have come alone
if you were worried.

01:00:34.714 --> 01:00:38.926
Si-woo's father
is hardly more than a parasite.

01:00:39.010 --> 01:00:40.136
He's got to go.

01:00:41.763 --> 01:00:44.557
Si-woo's cut him off a million times.

01:00:44.641 --> 01:00:47.518
Every time he tries, it doesn't last.

01:00:51.064 --> 01:00:52.899
Most people think you need your dad.

01:00:53.399 --> 01:00:55.902
For someone like Si-woo, though,
it's better being alone.

01:00:57.904 --> 01:01:00.907
[approaching footsteps]

01:01:01.866 --> 01:01:03.743
[Myung-han] Ah, Director Lady.

01:01:05.578 --> 01:01:06.913
There you are.

01:01:08.331 --> 01:01:09.791
So what's the deal?

01:01:13.503 --> 01:01:15.296
I was talking with that guy, the doctor.

01:01:17.090 --> 01:01:18.508
Si-woo could go blind.

01:01:20.468 --> 01:01:21.594
It's that bad?

01:01:21.678 --> 01:01:23.805
The explosion damaged the cornea.

01:01:23.888 --> 01:01:25.056
What do you think?

01:01:25.139 --> 01:01:28.559
His whole life ahead taken away,
'cause he's blind.

01:01:29.977 --> 01:01:34.440
If you don't get him what he's due,
make it right, I'm gonna do something.

01:01:35.400 --> 01:01:38.528
Don't try and pull a fast one
and try to cheap us out.

01:01:38.611 --> 01:01:41.614
'Cause I'll tell the government
you're dirty.

01:01:41.698 --> 01:01:43.616
And I'll tell any reporters, too.

01:01:43.700 --> 01:01:45.034
Understand?

01:01:45.118 --> 01:01:47.662
[sucks teeth]
If you make me do that…

01:01:47.745 --> 01:01:48.996
[clicks tongue]

01:01:49.080 --> 01:01:53.626
I'm gonna have to fire both you
and that guy, right?

01:01:54.502 --> 01:01:57.422
So don't think you can brush this
under the rug.

01:01:57.505 --> 01:02:00.591
Once you pay up, I'll go away.
Is that clear?

01:02:00.675 --> 01:02:04.262
[approaching footsteps]

01:02:04.846 --> 01:02:06.514
I'm the person you should be talking to.

01:02:09.600 --> 01:02:11.394
Mind your own beeswax.

01:02:11.477 --> 01:02:13.563
Well, I'm a spokesperson for the KMA.

01:02:14.147 --> 01:02:16.399
This is my beeswax,
'cause I handle the press

01:02:16.482 --> 01:02:18.693
- and relations with civilians.
- [scoffs]

01:02:18.776 --> 01:02:20.528
I came just to talk with you.

01:02:22.405 --> 01:02:24.407
[breathes deeply]

01:02:24.490 --> 01:02:26.367
- So let's talk.
- Damn it!

01:02:27.243 --> 01:02:28.536
Don't waste my time.

01:02:28.619 --> 01:02:30.580
You call up the head guy.

01:02:30.663 --> 01:02:33.666
Tell him to cut a check. Go. Go on.

01:02:34.167 --> 01:02:36.461
[Myung-han] I don't have all day. Go call.

01:02:36.544 --> 01:02:39.464
Now that I've seen my boy,
we need no less than 30 mill, okay?

01:02:39.547 --> 01:02:40.548
Capisce?

01:02:41.048 --> 01:02:42.467
Don't waste any more of my time.

01:02:42.550 --> 01:02:44.510
- Make the call.
- [Si-woo] That's enough!

01:02:45.052 --> 01:02:46.220
Huh?

01:02:47.138 --> 01:02:48.139
Hey.

01:02:51.684 --> 01:02:54.061
- [Si-woo] You're done.
- [Myung-han] Hey. Wait, wait.

01:02:54.145 --> 01:02:56.898
Hang on. Wait, wait, wait. Idiot.

01:02:56.981 --> 01:02:59.108
Why aren't you lying in bed? Play it up.

01:02:59.192 --> 01:03:01.611
I can't believe you're walking.
You'll lose us money.

01:03:02.236 --> 01:03:05.448
- You're done.
- Come on, you're throwing it all away.

01:03:05.531 --> 01:03:06.824
[Si-woo] I am.

01:03:06.908 --> 01:03:08.659
I'm ruining this chance for you.

01:03:08.743 --> 01:03:09.911
- Aren't I?
- What?

01:03:09.994 --> 01:03:11.996
What charity will this money go to?

01:03:12.580 --> 01:03:14.749
Gambling? Scamming?

01:03:14.832 --> 01:03:15.792
Call girls?

01:03:15.875 --> 01:03:17.335
What do you need it for?

01:03:17.960 --> 01:03:20.254
- You little--
- You've always been a disgrace!

01:03:20.338 --> 01:03:22.006
You're an embarrassment.

01:03:23.841 --> 01:03:28.387
And the least you could do for me
is go and never show your face! Go!

01:03:28.471 --> 01:03:30.640
- How dare you?
- [grunts]

01:03:30.723 --> 01:03:31.933
[gasps]

01:03:34.060 --> 01:03:35.478
[breathes heavily]

01:03:37.230 --> 01:03:39.357
[dramatic music]

01:03:56.249 --> 01:03:57.500
That boy.

01:03:58.376 --> 01:03:59.418
Damn it.

01:04:04.674 --> 01:04:05.758
Make it right.

01:04:06.676 --> 01:04:08.094
Thirty million won.

01:04:09.220 --> 01:04:10.054
Thirty mill.

01:04:23.359 --> 01:04:24.944
So you came here to negotiate?

01:04:25.653 --> 01:04:27.780
- Huh?
- Did you?

01:04:30.199 --> 01:04:31.075
I did…

01:04:37.748 --> 01:04:38.875
Yu-jin.

01:04:46.340 --> 01:04:47.466
[sighs]

01:04:53.431 --> 01:04:54.724
[exhales deeply]

01:04:58.352 --> 01:05:00.771
[male reporter] The 14th typhoon
of the season, Typhoon Ricky,

01:05:00.855 --> 01:05:03.691
is crossing the Korean peninsula
at a speed of 30m per hour.

01:05:03.774 --> 01:05:05.610
[raindrops pattering]

01:05:06.485 --> 01:05:07.778
Hey, talk to me.

01:05:09.655 --> 01:05:11.532
Or I'll talk to you.

01:05:15.578 --> 01:05:19.290
It was a mistake for me
to bring your father, I'm sorry.

01:05:19.373 --> 01:05:20.875
- But--
- [Si-woo] Some things

01:05:21.459 --> 01:05:23.210
aren't possible in this life.

01:05:25.171 --> 01:05:27.798
Like a person can never stop
a typhoon coming in.

01:05:29.133 --> 01:05:31.302
My dad isn't something you can change.

01:05:32.261 --> 01:05:33.930
That man will never…

01:05:35.181 --> 01:05:36.724
put in the work to change.

01:05:38.851 --> 01:05:40.853
I need to keep looking out for myself.

01:05:41.479 --> 01:05:43.356
I know you'll do the same thing, too.

01:05:48.903 --> 01:05:50.738
I've been thinking like you told me to.

01:05:53.532 --> 01:05:55.201
I thought about us every day.

01:05:59.538 --> 01:06:01.165
And I can't do what you want.

01:06:02.124 --> 01:06:04.043
I don't know what you're saying.

01:06:06.045 --> 01:06:08.631
["Love Hurts A Little More"
by Kim Na-young playing]

01:06:09.507 --> 01:06:13.344
[Ha-kyung] The warm air in a typhoon
means it's incredibly altered

01:06:13.427 --> 01:06:16.597
when it encounters cool air
as happens when it hits Korea.

01:06:17.598 --> 01:06:21.477
We call it a variation area.

01:06:26.816 --> 01:06:28.275
I have to let you go.

01:06:29.902 --> 01:06:31.654
I can't stay moderate.

01:06:35.700 --> 01:06:37.827
[Ha-kyung] Lee Si-woo,
has that typhoon warmth,

01:06:37.910 --> 01:06:40.413
when he met me, the cool air.

01:06:40.496 --> 01:06:45.960
Like a storm, he passed through,
and eventually had to say goodbye.

01:06:46.836 --> 01:06:49.088
["Love Hurts A Little More"
by Kim Na-young playing]

01:06:56.846 --> 01:06:57.888
Forgive me.

01:06:58.848 --> 01:07:00.182
I can't be what you want.

01:07:04.103 --> 01:07:05.312
So, let's…

01:07:08.941 --> 01:07:10.026
end it.

01:07:21.579 --> 01:07:23.039
[Ha-kyung] How did we end up

01:07:23.956 --> 01:07:29.086
looking down a path with no idea
of what awaits us?

01:07:36.010 --> 01:07:38.012
["Love Hurts A Little More"
by Kim Na-young playing]

01:08:02.161 --> 01:08:04.038
[Ha-kyung] Go back
to the hospital right now.

01:08:04.121 --> 01:08:06.499
I have no problem working.

01:08:06.582 --> 01:08:08.167
Is there a way for us to know sooner?

01:08:08.250 --> 01:08:09.877
[Mi-jin] We could launch a sonde
at the eastern side of Jeju

01:08:09.960 --> 01:08:11.420
and at the sea west of the island.

01:08:11.504 --> 01:08:13.297
But as you know,
it's too dangerous to go out

01:08:13.380 --> 01:08:16.050
into the sea in this weather
and to send out the sonde.

01:08:16.133 --> 01:08:17.218
[Bong-chan] We can only make predictions.

01:08:17.301 --> 01:08:20.179
There's no such thing
as an accurate forecast.

01:08:20.262 --> 01:08:22.139
[Ha-kyung]
Even if they're just predictions,

01:08:22.223 --> 01:08:23.849
I believe it is our duty to use

01:08:23.933 --> 01:08:26.393
the most accurate data possible
to make such predictions.

01:08:28.104 --> 01:08:30.314
You and I are married.
That's our conclusion.

01:08:30.397 --> 01:08:31.774
So tell me if you regret it.

01:08:31.857 --> 01:08:34.819
- Did you make my daughter cry?
- [Ki-jun] Sir, it's not what you think.

01:08:34.902 --> 01:08:37.780
[Seok-ho] I don't think I can do this.

01:08:37.863 --> 01:08:39.198
I can't see you, Tae-kyung.

01:08:39.281 --> 01:08:41.325
Let's break up, Si-woo.
